{
  "dom_id": "step-q318138",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "What number is $145%$ greater than $80?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find a number $145%$ *greater than* $80,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+145%=245%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n245%=\\frac{245}{100}=2.45\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $145%$ greater than $80,$ we multiply $80$ by $2.45:$\n\n$$\n2.45\\cdot 80=196\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $145%$ greater than $80$ is $196.$",
